# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000370  -  CAT II
# For devices and hosts within the scope of coverage, the Central Log Server
# must be configured to automatically aggregate events that indicate account
# actions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000370
group:           V-206516
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    Splunk can bring account-action events from every device in scope together
                 by routing each input's data to a declared index and classifying the
                 events with event types, so a single search reaches all of them.

governs:         eventtypes.conf - Used to configure event types and their properties.
governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [] index non_empty
check:           eventtypes.conf [] search present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          inputs.conf [] index https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.2-configuration-file-reference/inputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Which events each sending device emits for account creation, modification,
                 disablement, and removal, carried by that device's own audit policy; the
                 application can only aggregate what it is sent.
external:        A props.conf or transforms.conf route that discards events to the null
                 queue would drop them before indexing; whether a given filter does so is a
                 per-deployment data-routing decision (props.conf.spec:1043,
                 transforms.conf.spec:241).

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-AU-000370 check text;
                 inputs.conf.spec:93 (index), inputs.conf.spec:128 (queue =
                 [parsingQueue|indexQueue]), eventtypes.conf.spec:36 ([<$EVENTTYPE>]),
                 eventtypes.conf.spec:51 (search)
finding:         Inputs do not declare the index their data lands in, or no event type
                 classifies account actions, so the application does not bring
                 account-action events together for the devices within its scope of
                 coverage.
